{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "02WI", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-representable-properties}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:602e692e2db70f0250d16306b0cfbc1046a2ed05f2c4035cd1c68502be2cf1d6", "source_text": "Properties of representable morphisms of presheaves", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1f6107c7a74df46cf09251b1c6349b1fe0b6034765aac962e377cebc0f476624", "unit_id": "tag:02WI:title"}
{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02WI", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7ccba419f2f963c6a2bcbd05dcb9c34eaafb6940de0bc8fda6c82e247f26ad02", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nHere is the definition that makes this work.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:87507983410d80f25ab0324e81f484c17317965f3cc2e5f59c5f28502af1bc7e", "unit_id": "tag:02WI:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "02WI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$a : F \\to G$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "MATH_0004": "$a$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\in \\Ob((\\Sch/S)_{fppf})$", "MATH_0007": "$\\xi \\in G(U)$", "MATH_0008": "$V_\\xi \\to U$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-definition-preserved-by-base-change}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{descent-definition-property-morphisms-local}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-relative-representable-property}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:174db2119269eac933b0231d42dc8b1cdedbb00214edd536e18d8ba2d81073dc", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f23f9132b75aaf2a632c045d754868f147af6fc135f3a97dff57dd778eff2fb5", "source_text": "With <MATH_0001>, and <MATH_0002> representable as above.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a property of morphisms of schemes which\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> is preserved under any base change,\nsee Schemes, Definition <REF_0001>,\nand\n<STRUCT_0003> is fppf local on the base, see\nDescent, Definition <REF_0002>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nIn this case we say that <MATH_0004> has <TEXTITOPEN_0001>property <MATH_0005><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if for every\n<MATH_0006> and\nany <MATH_0007> the resulting morphism of schemes\n<MATH_0008> has property <MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4eeec183c2238edacfd504b9034237def7cd945ec0d784943be196a946f286a2", "unit_id": "tag:025V:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02WI", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7ccba419f2f963c6a2bcbd05dcb9c34eaafb6940de0bc8fda6c82e247f26ad02", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIt is important to note that we will only use this definition for\nproperties of morphisms that are stable under base change, and\nlocal in the fppf topology on the base. This is\nnot because the definition doesn't make sense otherwise; rather it\nis because we may want to give a different definition which is\nbetter suited to the property we have in mind.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d53059372ce84eaf69ca0e96499cda60682c51632decc491720cd698c97e509c", "unit_id": "tag:02WI:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "02WI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}=$", "MATH_0002": "$F \\to G$", "MATH_0003": "$F$", "MATH_0004": "$G$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-relative-representable-property}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sites-definition-presheaves-injective-surjective}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{sites-definition-sheaves-injective-surjective}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-surjective-flat-locally-finite-presentation}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-warning}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:463746f4d821ee831be9509e5698cd19be8aaebc07191fa25df6a72c5004e111", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fa76118e58f8c97e90307e3c9caaa70d8af2f34d395fc1d9fb3fc9223fd8129e", "source_text": "Consider the property <MATH_0001>``surjective''.\nIn this case there could be some ambiguity if we say\n``let <MATH_0002> be a surjective map''.\nNamely, we could mean the notion defined\nin Definition <REF_0001>\nabove, or we could mean a surjective map of presheaves, see\nSites, Definition <REF_0002>,\nor, if both <MATH_0003> and <MATH_0004> are sheaves,\nwe could mean a surjective map of sheaves, see\nSites, Definition <REF_0003>.\nIf not mentioned otherwise when discussing morphisms of algebraic spaces\nwe will always mean the first. See\nLemma <REF_0004>\nfor a case where surjectivity implies surjectivity as a map of sheaves.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d18d9a39b2abd62bbb067df229abf9364cefd3753c99d55ec40c5012ac07b92f", "unit_id": "tag:02YN:statement"}
